// Orbit definitions for the hero animation.
// Each entry describes one periodic n-body solution: an SVG path (traced by the
// bodies), plus keyTimes/keyPoints so motion speed matches the real physics
// (equal time-steps mapped to the true, unequal arc-length covered per step).
//
// "Choreography" solutions (e.g. figure8) have every body trace one identical
// curve, so the orbit-level path/keyTimes/keyPoints are shared and only
// bodies[].begin differs. Non-choreography solutions (goggles, yinyang1,
// scallopedflower) give each body its own path/keyTimes/keyPoints instead,
// with begin left at 0.
//
// scallopedflower is unequal-mass (bodies a,b: mass 1; body c: mass ~0.439),
// discovered via Monte Carlo search seeded from a real mass ratio measured by
// tracking a Reddit r/physicsgifs video, then refined to a true closed orbit
// via Newton-Raphson (see chat history for the full process).
//
// To add another solution: verify real initial conditions first (see chat
// history for the process used on these), integrate it the same way, and push
// a new entry here. script.js picks one at random on page load.

